min": "Environ 20 min", "Take out": "À emporter", "Pay from": "Payer avec", "Add items to order": "Ajouter des articles à la commande", "Paid with itunda Pay": "Payé avec itunda Pay", "itunda Pay balance": "Solde itunda Pay", "Purchase history": "Historique des achats", "Create a product link": "Créer un lien produit", "Connect friends": "Retrouver des amis", "Check your points": "Consulter vos points", "Start a money transfer": "Lancer un transfert d’argent", "Look up a route in Maps": "Chercher un itinéraire dans Cartes", "Get itunda card": "Obtenir la carte itunda", "Card cashback": "Cashback carte", "Interest received": "Intérêts reçus", "Get your interest today": "Recevez vos intérêts aujourd’hui", "Interest accrued through yesterday": "Intérêts courus jusqu’à hier", "Report an issue with a transaction": "Signaler un problème de transaction", "Menus, prices and ratings are sample data.": "Les menus, prix et notes sont des données d’exemple.", "Menu and prices are sample data.": "Le menu et les prix sont des données d’exemple.", "Products, prices and merchants are sample data.": "Les produits, prix et marchands sont des données d’exemple.", "Offers are sample data.": "Les offres sont des données d’exemple.", "Sample rewards": "Récompenses d’exemple", "Sample group for this prototype.": "Groupe d’exemple pour ce prototype.", "Sample account for this prototype.": "Compte d’exemple pour ce prototype.", "Skip (prototype)": "Passer (prototype)", "Prototype: no real account was created.": "Prototype : aucun compte réel n’a été créé.", "Rate (sample)": "Taux (exemple)", "Dividend (sample)": "Dividende (exemple)", "Good": "Bon", "Tip": "Astuce", "Free check using alternative data. Sample score for this prototype, not a real credit report.": "Vérification gratuite à partir de données alternatives. Score d’exemple pour ce prototype, pas un vrai rapport de crédit.", "Paying bills on time through itunda lifts your score. Starting a savings goal helps too.": "Payer vos factures à temps avec itunda améliore votre score. Se fixer un objectif d’épargne aide aussi.", "Higher amounts unlock as your score improves. Sample terms for this prototype. No real loan is made.": "Les montants plus élevés se débloquent à mesure que votre score s’améliore. Conditions d’exemple pour ce prototype. Aucun vrai prêt n’est accordé.", "Sample dividend and terms for this prototype.": "Dividende et conditions d’exemple pour ce prototype.", "Own a part of your cooperative. Each share is 5,000 RWF and earns a dividend when the SACCO makes a surplus.": "Détenez une part de votre coopérative. Chaque part vaut 5,000 RWF et rapporte un dividende lorsque la SACCO dégage un excédent.", "Save a little every day for 31 days": "Épargnez un peu chaque jour pendant 31 jours", "The longer your daily streak, the higher your bonus rate, up to 10%.": "Plus votre série quotidienne est longue, plus votre taux bonus augmente, jusqu’à 10 %.", "itunda Bank is not a licensed bank. Sample copy for this prototype.": "itunda Bank n’est pas une banque agréée. Texte d’exemple pour ce prototype.", "Lock money for 12 months. We pay the interest upfront and hold the principal.": "Bloquez votre argent 12 mois. Nous versons les intérêts d’avance et conservons le capital.", "A shared account for family, church or a cooperative. Everyone can add money.": "Un compte partagé pour la famille, l’église ou une coopérative. Chacun peut y ajouter de l’argent.", "For under-18s. You stay in charge: you add money and set the spending limit.": "Pour les moins de 18 ans. Vous gardez le contrôle : vous ajoutez de l’argent et fixez la limite de dépenses.", "Rates and balances are sample data for this prototype.": "Les taux et les soldes sont des données d’exemple pour ce prototype.", "Order tracking and the rider are simulated for this prototype.": "Le suivi de commande et le livreur sont simulés pour ce prototype.", "Your rider · ★ 4.9": "Votre livreur · ★ 4.9", "Choose what itunda can notify you about.": "Choisissez ce dont itunda peut vous notifier.", "Your balance and payments will look like this. Pick the size that is easiest to read.": "Votre solde et vos paiements s’afficheront ainsi. Choisissez la taille la plus facile à lire.", "Devices signed in to your itunda account.": "Appareils connectés à votre compte itunda.", "A passkey uses your fingerprint, face or screen lock. It cannot be guessed or shared.": "Une clé d’accès utilise votre empreinte, votre visage ou le verrouillage d’écran. Elle ne peut ni être devinée ni être partagée.", "Last updated 1 October 2026": "Dernière mise à jour : 1er octobre 2026", "1 point = 1 RWF in Pay money": "1 point = 1 RWF dans Pay money", "Free soda with a meal · Expires 20 Oct": "Soda offert avec un repas · Expire le 20 oct.", "2 free rides · Expires 15 Nov": "2 trajets offerts · Expire le 15 nov.", "5% off any order · Expires 31 Oct": "5 % de réduction sur toute commande · Expire le 31 oct.", "3-day streak": "Série de 3 jours", "Tap Go, do the task, then come back and claim your points.": "Touchez Go, faites la tâche, puis revenez réclamer vos points.", "Finish all three tasks today for a 100 point bonus and a coupon.": "Terminez les trois tâches aujourd’hui pour un bonus de 100 points et un coupon.", "Pick one category to earn 3%": "Choisissez une catégorie pour gagner 3 %", "1% back on every itunda card purchase": "1 % de cashback sur chaque achat par carte itunda", "5% back when you pay with QR": "5 % de cashback en payant par QR", "You earn 3% on purchases made through a product link you shared.": "Vous gagnez 3 % sur les achats faits via un lien produit que vous avez partagé.", "People from your contacts who play on itunda.": "Des personnes de vos contacts qui jouent sur itunda.", "Money moves on its own from your Pay money. We skip a transfer if your balance is too low.": "L’argent part tout seul de votre Pay money. Nous sautons un transfert si votre solde est trop bas.", "Your score helps you qualify for loans. It is never sold.": "Votre score vous aide à obtenir des prêts. Il n’est jamais vendu.", "You can ask to see or correct your data at any time.": "Vous pouvez demander à consulter ou corriger vos données à tout moment.", "Covered up to RWF 500,000 per user": "Couvert jusqu’à RWF 500,000 par utilisateur", "Save 500 RWF today": "Épargner 500 RWF aujourd’hui", "itunda is not a licensed bank, and this is not real government deposit insurance. \"itunda Bank\" is itunda's own product name for these savings, SACCO/Ikimina, loan, and investment features, not a separate licensed banking entity.": "itunda n’est pas une banque agréée, et il ne s’agit pas d’une véritable assurance-dépôts publique. « itunda Bank » est le nom de produit propre à itunda pour ces fonctions d’épargne, SACCO/Ikimina, de prêt et d’investissement, et non une entité bancaire agréée distincte."},rw:{"up to 500 RWF": "Kugeza kuri 500 RWF", "See schedule": "Reba gahunda", "Deal of the Day": "Igicuruzwa cy’umunsi", "Bus Times": "Amasaha ya bisi", "Your points": "Amanota yawe", "Invite a friend": "Tumira inshuti", "Sign out": "Sohoka", "Change PIN": "Hindura PIN", "Enter your current PIN": "Andika PIN yawe y’ubu", "This phone": "Iyi telefoni", "How much?": "Angahe?", "You pay": "Wishyura", "You get": "Wakira", "Where to?": "Ujya he?", "3 months": "Amezi 3", "6 months": "Amezi 6", "12 months": "Amezi 12", "Menus, prices and ratings are sample data.": "Menu, ibiciro n’amanota ni urugero gusa."}},R={"fr": [["^(\\d+) left$", "Plus que $1"], ["^(\\d+)% off$", "−$1 %"], ["^Earn ([\\d,]+) RWF back$", "Gagnez $1 RWF de cashback"], ["^You can borrow up to ([\\d,]+) RWF with your score of (\\d+)\\.$", "Vous pouvez emprunter jusqu’à $1 RWF avec votre score de $2."], ["^Apply for ([\\d,]+) RWF$", "Demander $1 RWF"], ["^Arrives in (\\d+) to (\\d+) min$", "Arrivée dans $1 à $2 min"], ["^(\\d+) to (\\d+) min · ([\\d,]+) RWF delivery$", "$1 à $2 min · livraison $3 RWF"], ["^Estimated dividend: ([\\d,]+) RWF a year$", "Dividende estimé : $1 RWF par an"], ["^itunda.s reserve: (.+)$", "Réserve d’itunda : $1"], ["^(\\d+) weeks ago$", "Il y a $1 semaines"], ["^(\\d+) days ago$", "Il y a $1 jours"]]},NB='\u00a0';
const tr=()=>{const L=S.lang;if(L!=='fr'&&L!=='rw')return;const d=D[L],ph=document.getElementById('phone');if(!ph)return;
const w=document.createTreeWalker(ph,NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);let n;while(n=w.nextNode()){const v=n.nodeValue,t=v.trim();if(t.length<3||n.parentElement&&/^(SCRIPT|STYLE|TEXTAREA|INPUT)$/.test(n.parentElement.tagName))continue;
let o=d[t];if(!o&&R[L])for(const[p,r]of R[L]){const re=new RegExp(p);if(re.test(t)){o=t.replace(re,r);break}}
if(o){if(L==='fr')o=o.replace(/ ([?:%])/g,NB+'$1');n.nodeValue=v.replace(t,o)}}};
let q=0;const s=()=>{if(q)return;q=requestAnimationFrame(()=>{q=0;tr()})};
new MutationObserver(s).observe(document.getElementById('phone'),{childList:true,subtree:true});s()}
document.title=document.title.replace('v165','v166');
/* v167: one currency format and one brand spelling. Amounts read "842,300 RWF" everywhere (some screens had "RWF 842,300", "+RWF 100"), and the brand is always lowercase "itunda" (fr/rw and one en string had "Itunda"). Runs after the v166 text swap on every render, in all languages. */
{const fx=s=>{let o=s.replace(/\bRWF\s?(\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)/g,'$1 RWF').replace(/\bItunda\b/g,'itunda');if(S.lang==='fr')o=o.replace(/le portefeuille itunda/g,'le compte itunda');return o};
const run=()=>{const ph=document.getElementById('phone');if(!ph)return;const w=document.createTreeWalker(ph,NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);let n;
while(n=w.nextNode()){const p=n.parentElement;if(p&&/^(SCRIPT|STYLE|TEXTAREA)$/.test(p.tagName))continue;const v=n.nodeValue;if(v.indexOf('RWF')<0&&v.indexOf('Itunda')<0)continue;const o=fx(v);if(o!==v)n.nodeValue=o}};
let q=0;const s=()=>{if(q)return;q=requestAnimationFrame(()=>{q=0;run()})};
new MutationObserver(s).observe(document.getElementById('phone'),{childList:true,subtree:true});s()}
document.title=document.title.replace('v166','v167');
/* v168: order tracking showed two route maps. v97 added the live map with the status caption but the original static map was never removed. Drop the old one whenever the live map is present (pickup and cancelled orders have no live map and are unchanged). */
{const _m=screens.etrack;screens.etrack=()=>{const h=_m();if(h.indexOf('id="map97"')<0)return h;const d=document.createElement('div');d.innerHTML=h;
[...d.children].forEach(c=>{if(c.className==='pad'&&c.getAttribute('style')==='padding-top:16px'&&c.querySelector('svg')&&!c.textContent.trim())c.remove()});return d.innerHTML}}
document.title=document.title.replace('v167','v168');
/* v169: (1) toasts sat a fixed 100px from the bottom, so on screens with a taller footer or an open sheet they covered the main button and swallowed the tap (19 screens, e.g. Next, Send, Save, Buy, and Pay on the loan screen). The toast now picks the spot (above the footer or sheet, below the header, or the old position) that covers the fewest tappable controls. (2) Loan "Next due" read "15 of each month" in every language; now "The 15th of each month", with fr/rw. */
{const cov=t=>{const tr=t.getBoundingClientRect();let a=0;document.querySelectorAll('#phone button,#phone [onclick],#phone input').forEach(e=>{if(e.closest('.toast'))return;const r=e.getBoundingClientRect();if(!r.width||!r.height||r.height<28)return;const h=Math.min(r.bottom,tr.bottom)-Math.max(r.top,tr.top),w=Math.min(r.right,tr.right)-Math.max(r.left,tr.left);if(h>0&&w>0)a+=h*w});return a};
const place=t=>{const ph=document.getElementById('phone').getBoundingClientRect();let top=ph.bottom;
document.querySelectorAll('#phone .cta,#phone .tabs,#phone .sheet').forEach(e=>{const r=e.getBoundingClientRect();if(r.width&&r.height&&r.top<top&&r.top>ph.top+ph.height*.25)top=r.top});
const opts=[{b:Math.max(12,Math.round(ph.bottom-top+12))+'px',t:'auto'},{b:'auto',t:'76px'},{b:'100px',t:'auto'}];let best=0,bs=1e9;
opts.forEach((o,i)=>{t.style.bottom=o.b;t.style.top=o.t;const s=cov(t)+i*1;if(s<bs){bs=s;best=i}});t.style.bottom=opts[best].b;t.style.top=opts[best].t};
new MutationObserver(ms=>{for(const m of ms)for(const n of m.addedNodes)if(n.nodeType===1&&n.classList.contains('toast'))place(n)}).observe(document.getElementById('phone'),{childList:true});
const D15={en:'The 15th of each month',fr:'Le 15 de chaque mois',rw:'Ku itariki ya 15 buri kwezi'};
const fix=()=>{const ph=document.getElementById('phone');if(!ph)return;const w=document.createTreeWalker(ph,NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);let n;while(n=w.nextNode()){if(n.nodeValue.trim()==='15 of each month')n.nodeValue=D15[S.lang]||D15.en}};
let q=0;new MutationObserver(()=>{if(q)return;q=requestAnimationFrame(()=>{q=0;fix()})}).observe(document.getElementById('phone'),{childList:true,subtree:true})}
document.title=document.title.replace('v168','v169');
/* v170: (1) Restaurant menu: the "More to order" heading was glued onto the 5th dish inside an extra, never-closed .mi row, so the last dishes were laid out side by side and the screen scrolled sideways (all languages). The heading now sits between dishes 4 and 5 and every dish is its own row again. (2) fr: Preview and Start on the route screen ran 4px past the edge; they get a little less side padding. (3) rw: the Mini tab strip ran 3px wide; tabs may now shrink. */
{const st=document.createElement('style');st.id='v170';st.textContent='.cta>.btn[style*="padding:0 22px"]{padding:0 18px!important}.cta>span[style*="white-space:nowrap"]{min-width:0}.mtabs button{min-width:0;padding:0 2px;font-size:15px}';document.head.appendChild(st)}
document.title=document.title.replace('v169','v170');
/* v171: tap targets. Community like/reply/save/share buttons and author names were 24px tall, and the "See all" links on Home, Pay and other sections were 16px, which is easy to miss with a thumb. The look is unchanged; each now has an invisible hit area of about 44px (extra area stops short of neighbouring buttons). */
{const st=document.createElement('style');st.id='v171';st.textContent='#phone .act button,#phone button[onclick*="cmWho"],#phone .hct a,#phone .sech a{position:relative}#phone .act button::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-10px -3px}#phone button[onclick*="cmWho"]::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-10px -4px}#phone .hct a,#phone .sech a{cursor:pointer}#phone .hct a::after,#phone .sech a::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-14px -10px}';document.head.appendChild(st)}
document.title=document.title.replace('v170','v171');
/* v172: Shop. (1) The Shop/Eats switch was 30px tall; it gets a ~44px hit area (look unchanged). (2) Short labels wrapped badly: "Daily check-/in" on the earn tiles and a lone "offer" on the deal banner. Wrapping is now balanced so lines break evenly. */
{const st=document.createElement('style');st.id='v172';st.textContent='#phone .seg button{position:relative}#phone .seg button::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-7px -2px}#phone .mis span,#phone .bn>div>div{text-wrap:balance}';document.head.appendChild(st)}
document.title=document.title.replace('v171','v172');
/* v173: Shop filter row. The Filters chip was 44px tall next to 36px sort chips and sat 24px away from the first one (other chips are 8px apart), and the row had extra space above it. Filters now matches the other chips (36px, with a 44px invisible hit area), the gap is 8px, the space above is tighter, and the row sits 8px clear of the category chips. */
{const st=document.createElement('style');st.id='v173';st.textContent='#phone .v144row>#shfl,#phone .v144row>#shsort{padding-top:4px!important}#phone .v144row>#shfl .cch.sh5-b{min-height:0;height:36px;position:relative}#phone .v144row>#shfl .cch.sh5-b::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-4px -2px}#phone .v144row>#shsort{padding-left:8px}#phone .v144row>#shsort .cch{height:36px}#phone .v144row{margin-bottom:8px}';document.head.appendChild(st)}
document.title=document.title.replace('v172','v173');
/* v174: take the folds out. The accordion rows added in v158-v164 hid content behind repeated keywords (Pay with, Pay again, Send again, Recent activity, More; Bank's six sections; Transit's Top up, Ride history, About fares; Property "Search and filters"; Loan "Rate and interest") and made people open row after row to see what they needed. Everything is on the page again, in the order a person uses it, under one plain heading each. On Pay: "Pay with" is now "Pay from" and sits right under the payment code, "Pay again" and "Send again" are one row ("Pay or send again"), Recent activity shows its rows with See all beside the heading, and the old More list is "Manage" without the two rows that repeated something already on the page (Request money, Cash out). fr/rw strings are new and need native review. Transit: the fare note under About fares gets its side padding back, and the disabled pay button says what to do ("Top up below to pay") instead of just "Balance too low". */
{const t3=(e,r,f)=>S.lang==='rw'?r:S.lang==='fr'?f:e;
const st=document.createElement('style');st.id='v174';
st.textContent='.v174h{padding:28px 24px 6px;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.2px}.v174h+.sec,.v174h+.pad,.v174h+.chips,.v174h+.sech{padding-top:6px!important}.v174h+.sec>.sech:first-child{margin-top:0}.v174 .sec>.sech:empty{display:none}.v174 .chips{padding-bottom:4px}';
document.head.appendChild(st);
const fold=x=>{const sm=x.querySelector(':scope>summary');return sm&&/min-height:(52|48)px/.test(sm.getAttribute('style')||'')?sm:null};
const title=sm=>[...sm.childNodes].filter(n=>n.nodeType===3).map(n=>n.nodeValue).join('').trim();
const body=(x,sm)=>[...x.children].filter(c=>c!==sm).map(c=>c.tagName==='DIV'&&/margin:0 -24px/.test(c.getAttribute('style')||'')?c.innerHTML:c.outerHTML).join('');
const mk=(ti,inner)=>{const w=document.createElement('div');w.className='v174';w.innerHTML=(ti?'<div class="v174h">'+ti+'</div>':'')+inner;return w};
const unfold=h=>{if(h.indexOf('<details')<0)return h;const d=document.createElement('div');d.innerHTML=h;
 d.querySelectorAll('details').forEach(x=>{const sm=fold(x);if(!sm)return;const card=!/24px/.test(x.getAttribute('style')||'');x.replaceWith(mk(card?'':title(sm),body(x,sm)))});return d.innerHTML};
['bank','transit','hood','loan'].forEach(k=>{const f=screens[k];if(f)screens[k]=()=>unfold(f())});
{const _t=screens.transit;screens.transit=()=>{let h=_t();h=h.replace(/>Balance too low</,'>'+t3('Top up below to pay','Shyiramo amafaranga hepfo kugira ngo wishyure','Rechargez ci-dessous pour payer')+'<');
 const d=document.createElement('div');d.innerHTML=h;const hd=[...d.querySelectorAll('.v174h')].find(e=>e.nextElementSibling&&e.parentElement.className==='v174'&&e.nextElementSibling.tagName==='DIV'&&!e.nextElementSibling.classList.contains('pad')&&!/padding/.test(e.nextElementSibling.getAttribute('style')||'')&&e===[...d.querySelectorAll('.v174h')].pop());
 if(hd)hd.nextElementSibling.style.padding='0 24px 8px';return d.innerHTML}}
const _p=screens.pay;
screens.pay=()=>{const h=_p();if(h.indexOf('<details')<0)return h;const d=document.createElement('div');d.innerHTML=h;
 const top=[...d.children],ds=top.filter(e=>e.tagName==='DETAILS'&&fold(e));
 if(ds.length!==5||top.length<11)return unfold(h);
 const [wD,aD,sD,rD,mD]=ds,pre=top.filter(e=>e.tagName!=='DETAILS');
 const part=x=>{const sm=fold(x);return{ti:title(sm),el:(()=>{const w=document.createElement('div');w.innerHTML=body(x,sm);return w})()}};
 const W=part(wD),A=part(aD),S2=part(sD),R=part(rD),M=part(mD);
 const out=document.createElement('div');
 pre.slice(0,3).forEach(e=>out.appendChild(e));
 out.appendChild(mk(t3('Pay from','Ishyura uvanye','Payer depuis'),W.el.innerHTML));
 pre.slice(3).filter(e=>e.style.height!=='6px').forEach(e=>out.appendChild(e.classList.contains('agt')?mk(e.textContent.trim(),''):e));
 const ac=A.el.querySelector('.chips'),sc=S2.el.querySelector('.chips');
 if(ac&&sc){[...sc.children].forEach(c=>ac.appendChild(c));out.appendChild(mk(t3('Pay or send again','Ishyura cyangwa wohereze nanone','Payer ou envoyer à nouveau'),'<div class="chips" style="gap:14px;padding-top:6px">'+ac.innerHTML+'</div>'))}
 else{out.appendChild(mk(A.ti,A.el.innerHTML));out.appendChild(mk(S2.ti,S2.el.innerHTML))}
 const sh=R.el.querySelector('.sech');if(sh)sh.insertBefore(document.createTextNode(R.ti),sh.firstChild);
 const rs=document.createElement('div');rs.className='v174';rs.innerHTML=R.el.innerHTML;out.appendChild(rs);
 const rows=[...M.el.querySelectorAll('.row')];const rq=rows.findIndex(r=>/reqSheet\(\)/.test(r.getAttribute('onclick')||''));
 if(rq>-1){const co=rows[rq+1];rows[rq].remove();if(co&&/soon\(\)/.test(co.getAttribute('onclick')||''))co.remove()}
 out.appendChild(mk(t3('Manage','Gucunga','Gérer'),M.el.innerHTML));
 return out.innerHTML};
document.title=document.title.replace('v173','v174')}
/* v175: Send, step 1 (who). The "phone or account number" field was only a picture of a field: you could not type in it, and its gray example (0781 234 567) looked like a real number someone had already filled in. It is now a real field with an example that reads as one ("e.g. 0781 234 567"), a hint under it that tells you what is needed and how far along you are ("Type a number, or pick someone below." / "6 of 10 digits" / "Looks good. Tap Next."), and a red message when the number cannot be right. Next switches on as soon as the number is valid, and typing a number that has been reported shows the same caution as picking it from Contacts. The hint under the disabled button now says what to do ("Pick a contact or type a number to continue."). fr/rw: amount screen names the person ("Vers Eric M. · 0781 234 567") like English does. New fr/rw strings need native review. */
{const t3=(e,r,f)=>S.lang==='rw'?r:S.lang==='fr'?f:e,C={'0788 000 214':'Amina K.','0781 234 567':'Eric M.'},BAD='0781 234 567';
const fmtP=d=>d.length>7?d.slice(0,4)+' '+d.slice(4,7)+' '+d.slice(7):d.length>4?d.slice(0,4)+' '+d.slice(4):d;
const msg=(d,ok)=>{if(!d.length)return[t3('Enter their 10-digit phone number, or tap a contact below.','Andika nimero cyangwa uhitemo umuntu hepfo.','Saisissez un numéro ou choisissez quelqu’un ci-dessous.'),0];
 if(d.length>=2&&d.slice(0,2)!=='07')return[t3('Phone numbers start with 07. Example: 0788 123 456.','Nimero za telefoni zitangira na 07.','Les numéros de téléphone commencent par 07.'),1];
 if(d.length>=3&&!/^07[2389]/.test(d))return[t3('That doesn’t look right. Numbers start with 072, 073, 078 or 079.','Iyi nimero ntisa neza. Yongere uyisuzume.','Ce numéro semble incorrect. Vérifiez-le.'),1];
 if(ok){const n=C[fmtP(d)];return[(n?n+' · ':'')+t3('Looks good. Tap ','Birasa neza. Kanda ','Parfait. Appuyez sur ')+t('nx')+'.',2]}
 return[t3((10-d.length)+' more digit'+(10-d.length===1?'':'s')+' to go','Imibare '+d.length+' kuri 10',d.length+' chiffres sur 10'),0]};
window.rcIn=el=>{const d=el.value.replace(/\D/g,'').slice(0,10),f=fmtP(d),ok=/^07[2389]\d{7}$/.test(d),was=!!S.flagged;el.value=f;S.rcd=f;S.to=ok?f:'';S.flagged=ok&&f===BAD;
 const m=document.getElementById('rch'),[tx,k]=msg(d,ok);if(m){m.textContent=tx;m.style.color=k===1?'var(--er)':k===2?'var(--ok)':'var(--mu)'}
 const b=document.querySelector('#phone .cta .btn');if(b)b.disabled=!ok;
